---
# Starlight's <TabItem> (user-components/TabItem.astro): {% tab "C#", icon: "seti:c-sharp" %}...{% endtab %}, inside
# {% tabs %} or {% os_tabs %}. Renders a panel that the tabs client script completes (ids, aria-labelledby, hidden):
# see tabs.liquid. `label` is required (Starlight throws without it). `id` ("csharp", "typescript") is accepted and
# written as data-tab-id: Starlight's TabItem has no such prop; the site's remark plugin used it to put the TypeScript
# tab first, which the converter did in the source order.
block: true
args: [label]
params: [icon, id]
---
<div role="tabpanel" data-label="{{ label | escape }}"{% if icon %} data-icon="{{ icon | escape }}"{% endif %}{% if id %} data-tab-id="{{ id | escape }}"{% endif %}>{{ body | strip }}</div>